 "verdict": "The learned model beats the reading-outside-band threshold rule on later missions, but it does NOT clearly beat the simpler rule 'the action failed': at its own threshold it flags much the same actions, and its small PR-AUC edge is within what one or two rows would change. Held-out missions M020 to M027 (80 actions, 12 with an anomaly): model precision 7/8, recall 7/12, PR-AUC 0.65; status rule precision 7/8, recall 7/12, PR-AUC 0.57; reading-outside-band rule precision 3/3, recall 3/12, PR-AUC 0.36. Rolling cuts pooled (180 actions, 25 anomalies): model precision 17/30, recall 17/25, PR-AUC 0.57; status rule precision 19/30, recall 19/25, PR-AUC 0.51; band rule precision 5/9, recall 5/25, PR-AUC 0.22. Among successful actions only (72 held out, 5 anomalies), the model's PR-AUC is 0.10 against a base rate of 0.07: no better than chance, so it does not find anomalies the rules miss. It is used to order ties in the queue and to explain a flag, never to raise one on its own. With this few anomalies every number here moves a lot with one row."
